  "prompt": "A game shows the score needed to make its top-k leaderboard: after each new score is added, return the k-th largest score seen so far.\n\n- Implement the Leaderboard class: the constructor receives k and the initial scores nums; add(score) records a score and returns the current k-th largest (duplicates count separately).\n- runLeaderboard / run_leaderboard (already written) builds a Leaderboard(k, nums), calls add for each value in adds, and returns the list of results.\n- 1 <= k <= 10,000; len(nums) >= k - 1, so at least k scores exist after every add. Up to 10,000 initial scores and 10,000 adds; scores are integers between -10^4 and 10^4.",
  "function": {
    "js": "runLeaderboard",
    "py": "run_leaderboard"
  },
  "starter": {
    "js": "class Leaderboard {\n  constructor(k, nums) {\n    // Your setup here\n  }\n\n  add(score) {\n    // Your code here\n  }\n}\n\nfunction runLeaderboard(k, nums, adds) {\n  const board = new Leaderboard(k, nums)\n  return adds.map(score => board.add(score))\n}\n",
    "py": "class Leaderboard:\n    def __init__(self, k, nums):\n        pass  # Your setup here\n\n    def add(self, score):\n        pass  # Your code here\n\n\ndef run_leaderboard(k, nums, adds):\n    board = Leaderboard(k, nums)\n    return [board.add(score) for score in adds]\n"
  },
